CORE
main.py
--unwind 2

^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[python-unbound-local\.\d+\] .*local variable 'x' referenced before assignment \(UnboundLocalError\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §12b. A name assigned anywhere in a function is local
for the whole function; reading it before the binding is an
UnboundLocalError. A pre-scan collects locally-assigned names and a
read before the local symbol exists emits a python-unbound-local
property instead of silently resolving the module global.
